# SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT OR Apache-2.0
#
# Generated wasm-bindgen artifacts are NEVER committed — they are reproducible
# from build-wasm.sh (which pins the CLI version to the wasm-bindgen crate in
# Cargo.lock). Committing a binary blob would be an unauditable, unreproducible
# trust hole for a security product. Rebuild locally instead.
#
# TRACKED (do not add here): build-wasm.sh, postern-sdk.js (the hand-written
# loader — hyphenated), README.md.
#
# IGNORED: the wasm module + the wasm-bindgen `--target web` glue it emits
# (crate lib name is `postern_sdk`, underscored — distinct from the loader).

# default --out-dir used by build-wasm.sh
/pkg/

# defensive: the glue filenames, in case a build writes them next to the loader
postern_sdk.js
postern_sdk.d.ts
postern_sdk_bg.wasm
postern_sdk_bg.wasm.d.ts
postern_sdk_bg.js
package.json
